.Dd July 3, 2026
.Dt XTC_DIO_SCHED 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_dio_sched_create ,
.Nm xtc_dio_sched_destroy ,
.Nm xtc_dio_sched_current ,
.Nm xtc_dio_sched_report ,
.Nm xtc_dio_sched_report_multi ,
.Nm xtc_dio_sched_best ,
.Nm xtc_dio_sched_mutation_rate ,
.Nm xtc_dio_sched_generation
.Nd adaptive genetic-algorithm tuner for runtime self-tuning
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.In xtc_dio_sched.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_create "const xtc_dio_sched_spec_t *spec" "xtc_dio_sched_t **out"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_destroy "xtc_dio_sched_t *g"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_current "const xtc_dio_sched_t *g" "int *out_genes"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_report "xtc_dio_sched_t *g" "double fitness"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_report_multi "xtc_dio_sched_t *g" "const double *fitness" "int n"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_best "const xtc_dio_sched_t *g" "int *out_genes" "double *out_fitness"
.Ft double
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_mutation_rate "const xtc_dio_sched_t *g"
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_generation "const xtc_dio_sched_t *g"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_dio_sched
is a small genetic-algorithm tuner for runtime self-tuning of integer
.Dq genes
(tunables) against an observed fitness, after Jake Moilanen's genetic
scheduler (OLS 2005).  A population of candidate gene-sets is
evaluated, the best are bred (elitism + per-gene crossover +
mutation), and the mutation rate
.Em adapts :
it falls while fitness improves (hone in) and rises when fitness drops
(a workload shift), so the tuner re-converges quickly; it is capped at
45% to keep it from thrashing.
.Pp
It is a pure, deterministic (seeded) optimiser with no I/O of its own:
the caller reads the current candidate's genes, uses them for one
evaluation window, and reports the fitness it observed.  The
.Xr xtc_iosched 3
write scheduler drives it with throughput fitness; the unit tests
drive it with a synthetic function.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_create
creates a tuner from
.Fa spec :
.Fa n_genes
(1 ..
.Dv XTC_DIO_SCHED_MAX_GENES ) ,
per-gene inclusive
.Fa min Ns / Ns Fa max
bounds and
.Fa init
seed candidate, the
.Fa population
size (>= 2), and the PRNG
.Fa seed .
Optionally the genes are partitioned into
.Fa n_phenos
phenotypes -- gene groups each tuned by their own fitness measure via
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_report_multi ;
.Fa n_phenos
<= 1 is the single-fitness case.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_current
copies the genes of the candidate currently under evaluation into
.Fa out_genes
.Pf ( Fa n_genes
ints); use these until the next report.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_report
reports the
.Fa fitness
observed while using the current candidate (higher is better),
advances to the next candidate, and -- when the whole population has
been evaluated -- breeds the next generation and adapts the mutation
rate.
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_report_multi
reports one fitness per phenotype
.Pf ( Fa n
must equal the configured
.Fa n_phenos ) ;
each phenotype advances and breeds its own genes independently.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_best
returns the best gene-set found so far into
.Fa out_genes
and its fitness into
.Fa out_fitness
(either pointer may be
.Dv NULL ) --
the set to use once tuning has converged.
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_mutation_rate
and
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_generation
return the current adaptive mutation rate and generation counter for
observability.
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_destroy
frees the tuner.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_dio_sched_create
returns
.Dv XTC_OK
on success or a negative
.Dv XTC_E_*
code.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_iosched 3
.Sh AUTHORS
.An The XTC Project .
